                <pb facs="0196" n="94" sameAs="frus:frus1919v01/pg94"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">714.1515/70: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Guatemala</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Thurston</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Guatemala</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1918-01-29T15:00:00-06:36"><hi rendition="#italic">January 29,
                                1918, 3 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[<hi rendition="#italic">Received 10.28
                            p.m.</hi>]</dateline></opener>
                <p>My telegram of January 28, 12 noon. The Minister for Foreign Affairs called this
                    morning to inform me that the Cuyamel Company’s laborers are armed and continue
                    development work.</p>
                <p>I have heard that Ocaña left Tegucigalpa because of objectionable treatment and
                    that the departure from here of the Honduranean Minister is due to his having
                    been recalled.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Thurston</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
